From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Patrick Quinn <patrick.jm.quinn@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 09:19:50 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] media: i2c: imx111: Derive the data depth from the requested
 format

imx111_set_pad_format() computes the data depth, and from it the pixel
rate, from the pad's current format before that format is updated, so
switching between RAW8 and RAW10 programs the depth of the previous
format. Use the format being set.

Signed-off-by: Patrick Quinn <patrick.jm.quinn@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/media/i2c/imx111.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/i2c/imx111.c b/drivers/media/i2c/imx111.c
index 073efc0f..d0a72f3c 100644
--- a/drivers/media/i2c/imx111.c
+++ b/drivers/media/i2c/imx111.c
@@ -1140,7 +1140,7 @@ static int imx111_set_format(struct v4l2_subdev *sd,
 		int ret;
 
 		sensor->cur_mode = mode;
-		sensor->data_depth = imx111_get_format_bpp(fmt);
+		sensor->data_depth = imx111_get_format_bpp(mbus_fmt);
 
 		ret = __v4l2_ctrl_s_ctrl_int64(sensor->pixel_rate,
 					       div_u64(sensor->pixel_clk_raw,
